### 4.3 Phase 3 — Web Vulnerability Scan (Nikto)

**Target(s):** http://172.17.0.2/ (DVWA, identified as the sole web server in Phase 1)

**Command used:**
```
nikto -h http://172.17.0.2 -o nikto_results.txt
```

**Scan stats:** 8,069 requests sent, 16 items reported, completed in 347 seconds (2026-08-13 21:22–21:28)

**Findings summary:**

| Finding | Detail | Severity |
|---|---|---|
| Directory indexing on `/config/` | File listing of the config directory is publicly browsable — a common location for DB credentials, secrets, and app config | High |
| Configuration information potentially accessible on `/config/` | Nikto flags this path as a likely source of remotely-readable config data | High |
| Directory indexing on `/docs/` | Documentation folder browsable — lower sensitivity than `/config/` but still unintended disclosure | Low |
| PHPSESSID cookie missing `HttpOnly` flag | Session cookie readable via JavaScript, increasing session-hijack risk if combined with an XSS vulnerability | Medium |
| Apache/2.4.25 confirmed outdated (current ≥2.4.66) | Corroborates the Nmap finding (F-001) via an independent tool | *(cross-referenced to F-001)* |
| Missing security headers (HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, CSP, Permissions-Policy) | Standard browser-side hardening headers absent; each individually low-impact but weakens defense-in-depth | Low |
| `.gitignore` file exposed | Discloses information about the project's directory/file structure to an attacker | Low |
| `/icons/README`, `/login.php` discovered | Default Apache file and expected admin login page — expected in this environment | Info |

