## 5. Findings Register

| Finding ID | Description | Severity | Affected Asset | Recommended Fix |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| F-001 | Apache httpd 2.4.25 in use (current ≥2.4.66); confirmed outdated by both Nmap and Nikto | Medium | 172.17.0.2:80 | Upgrade to a currently supported Apache release, or verify and document the Debian security-patch backport level |
| F-002 | SSH management service reachable from the container/bridge network segment | Low | 172.17.0.1:22 | Restrict SSH exposure to management-only network segments; disable password auth in favor of key-based auth |
| F-003 | DVWA login form transmits credentials (`username`, `password`) and CSRF token in cleartext over unencrypted HTTP — confirmed via Wireshark packet capture (frame 35) | Critical | 172.17.0.2 (DVWA login) | Enforce HTTPS/TLS site-wide; redirect HTTP to HTTPS; enable HSTS; ensure session cookies use the `Secure` flag once TLS is in place |
| F-004 | Directory indexing enabled on `/config/`, with configuration information potentially readable | High | 172.17.0.2:80 (/config/) | Disable directory indexing; move sensitive config files outside the web root or restrict via server config |
| F-005 | Directory indexing enabled on `/docs/` | Low | 172.17.0.2:80 (/docs/) | Disable directory indexing in Apache config (`Options -Indexes`) |
| F-006 | Session cookie (PHPSESSID) set without the `HttpOnly` flag | Medium | 172.17.0.2:80 | Set `HttpOnly` (and `Secure`, once HTTPS is enforced) on session cookies |
| F-007 | Missing recommended security headers (HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, CSP, Permissions-Policy) | Low | 172.17.0.2:80 | Add the missing headers via Apache config or application middleware |
| F-008 | `.gitignore` file exposed, revealing directory structure | Low | 172.17.0.2:80 (/.gitignore) | Remove build/deployment artifacts like `.gitignore` from the publicly served web root |

