## 7. Conclusion

This assessment identified 8 findings across the DVWA test environment, ranging from one Critical exposure (cleartext login credentials) to several lower-severity hardening opportunities. The environment's overall posture reflects its purpose as an intentionally vulnerable training target — the findings here mirror the kinds of real-world misconfigurations (unencrypted authentication, exposed configuration directories, outdated software, missing security headers) that this assessment methodology is designed to catch before they reach production. All testing was conducted in a controlled, self-owned Docker/Kali lab for skills-development purposes, with no third-party or production systems involved.

